msgid "Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/25-component_relay.rst:111
msgid "Setting up the relay pin: - The relay module is connected to pin 6 of the Arduino. This pin is defined as ``relayPin`` for ease of reference in the code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/25-component_relay.rst:118
msgid "Configuring the relay pin as an output: - In the ``setup()`` function, the relay pin is set as an OUTPUT using the ``pinMode()`` function. This means the Arduino will send signals (either HIGH or LOW) to this pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/25-component_relay.rst:127
msgid "Toggling the relay ON and OFF: - In the ``loop()`` function, the relay is first set to the OFF state using ``digitalWrite(relayPin, LOW)``. It remains in this state for 3 seconds (``delay(3000)``). - Then, the relay is set to the ON state using ``digitalWrite(relayPin, HIGH)``. Again, it remains in this state for 3 seconds. - This cycle repeats indefinitely."
msgstr ""

